  "prefLabel": "Ph 705.04 Authorization for Destruction of Non-Inventory Controlled Substances",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 705.04 Authorization for Destruction of Non-Inventory Controlled Substances.\n\n(a) Subject to (b) through (d), below, any person legally possessing non-inventory controlled substances who wishes to dispose of the substances shall request authorization from the board to destroy the substances in accordance with Ph 705.05.\n\n(b) A consultant pharmacist shall be deemed to be an agent of the board for purposes of destroying non-inventory controlled substances at the institution for which the individual serves as consultant pharmacist without requesting prior authorization under Ph 705.05.\n\n(c) A pharmacist at an institution having an on-site pharmacy other than, or in addition to, an automated pharmacy system shall be deemed to be an agent of the board for purposes of destroying non-inventory controlled substances at the institution for which the individual works as a pharmacist without requesting prior authorization under Ph 705.05.\n\n(d) An individual designated as the board’s agent and so authorized by (b) or (c), above, to destroy non-inventory controlled substances shall comply with Ph 705.06 relative to having a witness and making a record of the destruction, and may designate another responsible individual to conduct the actual destruction.\n\nSource. #14648, eff 10-13-26, EXPIRES: 10-13-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html"
}
